All,

Upshot of what follows is that PE pipe is more expensive than PVC pipe.  Fo=
r main sizes the PE is about 20% more than PVC.  For lateral sizes the diff=
erence is about 10%.  This feeds into the PVC mains/ PE laterals narrative.=
  Note that there are a lot of glue joints to make when using PVC laterals =
than there will be fusion joints for PE laterals.  Bear in mind that input =
commodity prices can swing PVC and PE in opposite directions.

Here is an overview of the costs of PE versus PVC from a distributor that d=
oes this on a continent wide basis.  Freight costs are included.

All costs are Distributor costs per foot.  At this time.

For 6" IPS:

PE DR13.5 - For larger orders to smaller orders.  $3.10 to $3.40

PVC SDR21 - $2.50 to $2.80

For 2" IPS:

PE DR13.5 - $.41 to $.52

PVC SDR21 - $.37 to $.40

PVC prices are more consistent.  PE prices "jumps around" 6% to 8% in part =
as a result of plant location (freight) effects.  Note there are a lot more=
 plants making PVC pipe so the likelihood of having a closer source and low=
er freight costs are higher for PVC.

Although a secondary cost effect, this distributor seeks these economies.  =
PE has shape issues when filling trucks.  With 40 foot sticks and small dia=
meter pipe in coils trucks cannot be filled as efficiently.  It is much eas=
ier to fill out a partial truck load of pipe when it is PVC than when it is=
 PE.

J


